# CR 111.13, 707.10f: the token a copy of a permanent spell becomes as it resolves is not created, so Elspeth, Storm Slayer's
# "if one or more tokens would be created under your control" does not apply to it. Bot1 puts Elspeth onto the battlefield on
# turn 1 (Mox Pearl and Plains for her white, three more Moxen), and on turn 3 sacrifices Black Lotus for its mana to cast
# Uldaros Theorix, whose ability exiles the Lotus from the graveyard and casts a copy of it: exactly one Black Lotus token, where
# Elspeth would have made two of a token that was created.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Elspeth, Storm Slayer
Uldaros Theorix
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

